description:
Search the current credential's Xquik OpenAPI catalog for X (Twitter) operations. The sandbox has no network access. spec is global and the async function's first argument. spec.paths maps paths to HTTP methods and operation objects. Fields include operationId, summary, description, readOnly, tags, parameters, requestBody, and responses. The catalog resolves inputs inline. Each response schema describes the body as the API sends it and execute's request() returns it. Response $refs point to reusable schemas in spec.components.schemas. An answer can hold operation descriptions, parameters & response schemas with their paths. Fields remain queryable independently. Answers hold up to 24,000 characters of JSON. Free.

Examples
```js
// Every tag
async (spec) => [...new Set(Object.values(spec.paths).flatMap(Object.values).flatMap((op) => op.tags ?? []))]
// Operations tagged Users
async (spec) => Object.entries(spec.paths).flatMap(([path, methods]) => Object.entries(methods).filter(([, op]) => op.tags?.includes("Users")).map(([method, op]) => ({ method, path, summary: op.summary })))
// 1 operation's parameters
async (spec) => Object.values(spec.paths).flatMap(Object.values).find((op) => op.operationId === "searchTweets")?.parameters
```
